.TH TUXDISPLAY 1 "September 2026" "TuxDisplay 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuxdisplay \- use an iPad as a USB-connected secondary Linux monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxdisplay
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TuxDisplay
creates a compositor-owned virtual monitor in a GNOME Wayland session and streams it to the OpenDisplay iPad app through usbmuxd. This direct USB mode requires no IP network, Internet connection, or Personal Hotspot. Windows can be dragged between the physical display and the iPad. An authenticated browser viewer and an isolated X11/noVNC workspace remain available as compatibility fallbacks.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start, stop, restart
Control the per-user display service.
.TP
.B status
Show service state, display mode, OpenDisplay connection state, browser fallback URL, and access PIN.
.TP
.B url
Print the preferred iPad URL.
.TP
.B password [--reset]
Show or regenerate the six-digit access PIN.
.TP
.B launch APPLICATION [ARGUMENT ...]
Start an application in the current desktop. In X11 fallback mode, start it in the isolated workspace.
.TP
.B usb connect|disconnect|status
Detect a trusted iPad, start direct OpenDisplay USB streaming, or manage a supported USB gadget fallback.
.TP
.B tray
Run the GNOME tray indicator with start, USB connect, and close-connection actions.
.TP
.B doctor
Check display mode, dependencies, networking, and USB gadget capability.
.TP
.B gui
Open the standalone GTK manager. This is the default when no command is given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuxdisplay/config
Resolution and port settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuxdisplay/password
Generated access PIN. The file is readable only by its user.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tuxdisplay/
Service state and application logs.
.SH SECURITY
OpenDisplay traffic uses the trusted local usbmuxd cable connection. Protocol version 3 has no additional authentication, so unlock the iPad and trust only computers you control. The browser fallback listens on all interfaces and uses PIN authentication over ordinary HTTP; do not expose port 6080 to the public Internet.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuxdisplay-usb (8)
